      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone August 14, 2026 — Treble Cone is open for a fine day on the mountain, with light winds and good coverage across the 98 cm snow base. The recent melt-freeze cycle has left the surface firm and fast first thing, while overnight grooming has prepared freshly corduroyed pistes for the morning. As the sun works on the snow, conditions should soften into more forgiving spring snow by midday. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Home Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access, Skinning Access and Powder Bowl are open, while Matukituki Basin, Motatapu Chutes and Sundance are closed. Big Skite is on hold among the groomed trails. The access road is chain-free, but all vehicles must carry chains. There is an active road hazard advisory on the access roads, so skiers should check conditions before travelling and consider the free road shuttle or carpooling. Treble Cone is open from 8:30am to 4pm.",
